    "# CS229 L05 — Gaussian Discriminant Analysis & Naive Bayes\n",
    "\n",
    "**Video:** Spring 2026 · [YouTube](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=zRdE8A4UZes)  \n",
    "**Instructor:** Chris Re  \n",
    "**Topics:** Generative vs. Discriminative · Multivariate Gaussian · GDA · MLE for GDA · Linear Decision Boundary · QDA · GDA vs. Logistic Regression · Naive Bayes · Laplace Smoothing\n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "> 📌 *Lecture:* \"These generative models are pretty interesting because they're the G in GPT. So you hear ChatGPT, it's Generative Pre-trained Transformers. We'll maybe do pre-training a little bit later, maybe transformers a little bit later, but today we're getting our first example of a generative algorithm.\"\n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "## Roadmap\n",
    "\n",
    "| Section | Key Idea |\n",
    "|---|---|\n",
    "| 1. Generative vs. Discriminative | Model $p(x,y)$ not just $p(y|x)$ |\n",
    "| 2. Multivariate Gaussian | Mean vector $\\mu$, covariance matrix $\\Sigma$ |\n",
    "| 3. GDA Setup | Class-conditional Gaussians, shared $\\Sigma$ |\n",
    "| 4. MLE for GDA | Closed-form: count and average — no gradient descent |\n",
    "| 5. Decision Boundary | Linear (shared $\\Sigma$) vs. quadratic (per-class $\\Sigma$) |\n",
    "| 6. GDA vs. Logistic Regression | GDA $\\Rightarrow$ logistic regression (not vice versa) |\n",
    "| 7. Naive Bayes | Conditional independence; $O(D)$ parameters instead of $O(2^D)$ |\n",
    "| 8. Laplace Smoothing | Prevent zero-probability features |\n"
   ]
