   "source": [
    "## 5. GDA Decision Boundary\n",
    "\n",
    "### Prediction rule\n",
    "\n",
    "Classify a new point $x$ by:\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\\hat{y} = \\arg\\max_y\\; p(x \\mid y)\\, p(y)\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "The **decision boundary** is where $p(x \\mid y=0)\\,p(y=0) = p(x \\mid y=1)\\,p(y=1)$, i.e., where the log-ratio equals zero.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Why shared $\\Sigma$ gives a linear boundary\n",
    "\n",
    "Expanding the Gaussian log-likelihood ratio:\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\\log \\frac{p(x|y=1)p(y=1)}{p(x|y=0)p(y=0)} = 0\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\\left[-\\frac{1}{2}(x-\\mu_1)^T\\Sigma^{-1}(x-\\mu_1)\\right] - \\left[-\\frac{1}{2}(x-\\mu_0)^T\\Sigma^{-1}(x-\\mu_0)\\right] + \\log\\frac{\\phi}{1-\\phi} = 0\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "Expanding the quadratic forms:\n",
    "$$\n",
    "x^T\\Sigma^{-1}x - 2\\mu_1^T\\Sigma^{-1}x + \\mu_1^T\\Sigma^{-1}\\mu_1 \\;-\\; x^T\\Sigma^{-1}x + 2\\mu_0^T\\Sigma^{-1}x - \\mu_0^T\\Sigma^{-1}\\mu_0 + \\log\\frac{\\phi}{1-\\phi} = 0\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "The **quadratic terms $x^T\\Sigma^{-1}x$ cancel** (because $\\Sigma$ is shared). What remains is:\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\\underbrace{(\\mu_1 - \\mu_0)^T\\Sigma^{-1}}_{\\theta^T} x = \\underbrace{\\frac{1}{2}(\\mu_1^T\\Sigma^{-1}\\mu_1 - \\mu_0^T\\Sigma^{-1}\\mu_0) - \\log\\frac{\\phi}{1-\\phi}}_{\\theta_0}\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "This is a **hyperplane** $\\theta^T x = \\theta_0$ — a linear decision boundary.\n",
    "\n",
    "> 📌 *Lecture:* \"The most important takeaway: GDA in its current form does have a decision boundary which is a line, even though it does all this nice probabilistic stuff underneath the covers.\"\n",
    "\n",
    "### QDA: different $\\Sigma$ per class → quadratic boundary\n",
    "\n",
    "If each class gets its own $\\Sigma_0$, $\\Sigma_1$, the quadratic terms **don't cancel**. The boundary becomes a quadratic (ellipse, hyperbola, parabola, etc.).\n",
    "\n",
    "| Model | $\\Sigma$ | Boundary | Parameters |\n",
    "|---|---|---|---|\n",
    "| GDA (LDA) | shared | Linear hyperplane | $O(d)$ means + one $\\Sigma$ |\n",
    "| QDA | per-class | Quadratic surface | $O(d)$ means + two $\\Sigma$'s |\n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "> 🎯 **Interview:** Why does GDA produce a linear decision boundary?\n",
    "> \n",
    "> **A:** When both classes share the same covariance matrix $\\Sigma$, the quadratic term $x^T \\Sigma^{-1} x$ appears identically on both sides of the log-likelihood ratio and cancels. What remains is linear in $x$, giving a hyperplane as the decision boundary. If classes have different covariances (QDA), these terms don't cancel and the boundary becomes quadratic.\n"
   ]
